Control: with MESA_GLSL_DISABLE_IO_OPT=1 and without the targeted NIR patch,
the full strict oracle also exited 0 on the physical AMD. That experiment
motivated the narrow linker patch. With the narrow patch, DRM shim NIR dump
shows the user VS's CLIP_DIST0 store without no_varying, while next_stage
remains MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT. The shim fixture linked its GLSL program and
completed its shader draw with GL error zero.

The two targeted physical runs completed before their 40s timeout. Kernel
journal filtered from first to last run had no GPU reset, ring timeout or
fault. Installed Mesa afterwards: direct rendering Yes, AMD radeonsi,
Mesa 25.2.8-0ubuntu0.24.04.4.

The private Mesa source and libgallium were restored byte-for-byte to their
pre-test state; the object archives were also rebuilt from restored sources.
Installed driver was not changed.
